---
description: Investigate the user's retained build or runtime question and compose an evidence-grounded finding and any requested private handoff.
args:
  goal: string
returns: BuildIncidentOutcome
---
Own the requested diagnostic or comparison. Discover the actual retained incident and select evidence relevant to the user's boundary. A build duration, compiler diagnostic, source inventory, initial payload and runtime memory observation establish different facts. Use the available checkpoint selection and assessment hierarchy to investigate what the request actually needs; independent applicable checkpoints may be assessed concurrently. Do not run an inapplicable build review just to fill an output field.

Keep exact checkpoint identities, observed diagnostics, measurement classes and revision distinctions with the assessment. Let decideFinding interpret the evidence and any unresolved boundary. An unavailable or incompatible checkpoint can support an honest explanation of what cannot be concluded; it cannot support a fabricated profile or a claim that a process was measured. Pass actual observations forward when refining the investigation.

Retain a private incident handoff only if the user's goal requests it and the native owner scope permits that exact evidence. Pass the actual disposition with the selected checkpoint identities to stageEvidence so the requested interpretation is retained with its native evidence, then consume the actual receipt or refusal. A recommendation to investigate later is not an effect already performed, and a permission is not an instruction to write. Return the actual current and baseline assessments used, or null when unavailable or not applicable, the requested disposition and only an actual retained handoff receipt.
